# oracle: fix rigid custom v_bid (an atom-style variable of the positions) over two runs: native evaluates the variable once, when the fix is defined, so the bodies keep their atoms in the second run although the atoms moved across the variable's steps (the engine re-evaluated it at each run's init and regrouped the atoms)
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.4e-14, atoms 1.2e-13. Before the fix the setup row of the second run had temp 0.18300 where native prints 0.25971.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-12
units           lj
lattice         sc 0.5
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
variable        bid atom floor(x/2.0)+3*floor(y/2.5)
fix             1 all rigid custom v_bid
variable        vx atom 0.3*sin(0.9*x+0.4*z)
variable        vy atom 0.3*cos(0.6*y+0.8*x)
variable        vz atom 0.3*sin(0.7*z-0.3*y)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
timestep        0.002
thermo_style    custom step temp pe ke etotal press f_1[1][1] f_1[1][4] f_1[4][7] f_1[2][13]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             60
run             20
